sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor U as User
    participant B as Browser
    participant N as NGINX
    participant P as OAuth2 Proxy (App 3)
    participant E as Microsoft Entra ID
    participant A as App 3 Container
    rect rgb(232,241,255)
    U->>B: Open App 3 URL
    B->>N: HTTPS GET app3.ctcore...
    N->>P: Route request to App 3 OAuth2 Proxy
    P->>P: Check session cookie
    alt No valid session
        P-->>B: 302 redirect to Entra authorize endpoint
        B->>E: Authorization request: client_id, redirect_uri, scopes, state
        E-->>U: Authenticate / SSO / MFA if required
        U-->>E: Complete authentication
        E-->>B: 302 redirect to App 3 callback with auth code
        B->>N: GET /oauth2/callback?code=...
        N->>P: Route callback to App 3 proxy
        P->>E: Exchange authorization code for tokens
        E-->>P: Return tokens / claims
        P-->>B: Set-Cookie secure session + redirect to original URL
        B->>N: Repeat original request with session cookie
        N->>P: Route request
    else Valid session exists
        P->>P: Validate session cookie
    end
    end
    rect rgb(232,247,239)
    P->>A: Forward authenticated request upstream
    A->>A: Enforce app-specific authorization/business rules
    A-->>P: Application response
    P-->>N: Return response
    N-->>B: HTTPS response
    B-->>U: Render App 3
    end
    Note over P,E: OAuth2 Proxy orchestrates the OIDC/OAuth flow; Entra authenticates.
    Note over P: Session cookie is created by the proxy and stored by the browser.
    Note over A: Authentication does not replace application authorization.